auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  Authentication

  Every request generated from the OpenAPI document carries `auth: inherit`,
  which means it takes the collection's auth — this file. Without it, `inherit`
  resolves to nothing and protected endpoints answer 401.

  To get a token:

  1. Select an environment (Local or Production) from the picker, top right.
  2. Run `auth / Exchange credentials for a bearer token`, filling in the email
     and password of an admin account.
  3. Copy `token` out of the response.
  4. Open the environment, paste it into `token`, and save.

  `token` is declared as a secret variable, so Bruno keeps it out of the
  environment file that is committed. It is a JWT and expires after seven days,
  so expect to repeat this occasionally — a sudden run of 401s usually means it
  has lapsed rather than anything being broken.

  This file is not regenerated by the OpenAPI sync, unlike the request files, so
  anything set here survives a re-sync.
}
